            <ArticleTitle>Multivalent dithiafulvenyl functionalization of dendritic oligo(phenylene vinylene)s with an anthraquinodimethane core.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1821-1824</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6cc10085f</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Redox-active dithiafulvenyl endgroups were attached to dendritic oligo(phenylene vinylene)s which contain a non-planar, twisted anthraquinodimethane core. The ability of these π-electron rich molecules to bind with nitrobenzene and its derivatives was demonstrated, and their electrochemically generated polymer thin films were tested as efficient sensors for nitrobenzene.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
